    "seoKeywords": "Next.js state management, Next.js API boundaries, server state vs client state, URL state, Route Handlers, Server Actions, Next.js web application architecture, state ownership, data fetching architecture",
    "seoDescription": "An architectural guide to state ownership and API boundaries in Next.js. Learn where state belongs, when to use Route Handlers vs direct server data access, and how to design clean data flow.",
    "excerpt": "An architectural decision framework for modern Next.js applications: categorizing state ownership, eliminating unnecessary API layers, and designing secure mutation boundaries.",
    "status": "published",
